## Current Body Text
{{ draft_text }}

## Editing Rules
1. Only edit current body text, do not redo plan, do not add main events.
2. Prioritize P0: word count, facts, prohibited changes, opening reception, closing exit.
3. If fixing language, preserve original plot outcomes and paragraph responsibilities; do not ruin causal chains for the sake of polishing.
4. Forbidden: adding non-planned POVs, behind-the-scenes perspectives, prohibited characters' positive actions, unplanned organizations/items/major revelations.
5. When word count is too short, add process, action, effective dialogue, and sensory anchors; when word count is too long, delete redundant explanations and low-information narration.
6. Delete system traces, planning terminology, report terminology, and metanarrative words.
7. After repair, full text must still satisfy `{{ render_word_constraint_self_check(chapter.target_word_count | default(target_word_count | default(0), true)) }}`.
8. When triggering repetition risk, prioritize compressing repetition channels: keep the one carrying new information, change the rest to action, dialogue, decision, or scene staging.
9. Do not add new details just because there are multiple sensory cues in the plan; only add details that can improve causality, relationship, or transition clarity.
10. Editing contract cards take priority over general style preferences: voice signature, symbol explanation, aftermath, and body signal budgets must be reflected in deletion/editing actions.
